<!--
  ============================================================================
  LOCAL CATALOG FEED : development & test fixture (NOT a real partner feed)
  ============================================================================
  (XML comments may not contain a double hyphen, so dividers use '=' below.)

  A deliberately MESSY Google Merchant RSS 2.0 feed that imitates what the real
  partner network (Admitad MENA / Impact / ArabyAds) will eventually send, while
  it is still in moderation. ONE file, used two ways, both through the real
  ImportFeedJob pipeline (parse, brand filter, upsert):
    * tests/Feature/LocalCatalogFeedTest.php  (integration test on real data)
    * `php artisan feed:seed-local`           (dev-only catalog seeder)

  It exercises, on purpose and interleaved:
    * allowed brands (Zara, Mango, Massimo Dutti, H&M, and the modest-wear labels
      Bouguessa, Modanisa) and foreign ones that the JOB's brand allow-list must
      drop (Nike, Adidas);
    * prices in several shapes: "149.00 AED", "AED 249.00", "1,499.00 AED",
      a foreign currency, and an unparseable one;
    * categories as Google taxonomy, as free text, and one that maps to nothing;
    * all three target categories among the survivors (upper_body, lower_body, dresses);
    * repeated tags (g:size twice) and nesting (g:shipping) to prove the full
      structural snapshot lands in products.raw losslessly;
    * items WITH the g: prefix and items WITHOUT it;
    * the product image under different field names (image_link / picture / photo);
    * several broken/incomplete items (missing a required field) mixed in.

  ============================================================================
  TRUTH TABLE : what the import does with each <item> and why
  (the tests assert exactly this)
  ============================================================================
   id                | brand         | outcome             | reason
   ZARA-SHIRT-01     | Zara          | IMPORTED upper_body | valid; g:-prefixed; image_link
   NIKE-LEG-05       | Nike          | FILTERED (brand)    | parses fine, brand not allowed
   MANGO-DRESS-02    | Mango         | IMPORTED dresses    | "1,499.00 AED"; image via g:picture;
                     |               |                     | repeated g:size + nested g:shipping
   ZARA-USD-07       | Zara          | SKIPPED (parser)    | price "99.00 USD" (foreign currency)
   MD-TROUSER-03     | Massimo Dutti | IMPORTED lower_body | NO g: prefix; "AED 249.00";
                     |               |                     | free-text category; image via photo
   MANGO-BAG-09      | Mango         | SKIPPED (parser)    | category "Handbags" maps to nothing
   HM-TOP-04         | H&M           | IMPORTED upper_body | "79.00 AED"; category via product_type
   ZARA-NOIMG-11     | Zara          | SKIPPED (parser)    | no image_link/picture/photo (required)
   ADIDAS-JACKET-06  | Adidas        | FILTERED (brand)    | parses fine, brand not allowed
   ZARA-SALE-08      | Zara          | SKIPPED (parser)    | price "Sale" (unparseable amount)
   ZARA-NOID-10      | Zara          | SKIPPED (parser)    | missing <id> (required field)
   BOUG-ABAYA-12     | Bouguessa     | IMPORTED dresses    | modest wear; taxonomy "Abayas"
   MODA-HIJAB-14     | Modanisa      | IMPORTED upper_body | modest wear; product_type "Hijabs"
   MODA-SHAYLA-15    | Modanisa      | IMPORTED upper_body | modest wear; product_type "Shaylas"

   Totals: 14 items, 7 imported, 2 brand-filtered, 5 parser-skipped.
   Imported categories: upper_body x4 (ZARA-SHIRT-01, HM-TOP-04, MODA-HIJAB-14,
                                       MODA-SHAYLA-15),
                        lower_body x1 (MD-TROUSER-03),
                        dresses    x2 (MANGO-DRESS-02, BOUG-ABAYA-12).

  ============================================================================
  NOTE ON flat_bg_verified : intentionally NOT decided here
  ============================================================================
  Whether a product photo is a clean flat-lay (usable for VTON) vs a photo on a
  model is something only the LIVE feed's real images can tell. The image URLs
  below are placeholders, so this fixture says nothing about flat_bg_verified:
  the verifier stays a stub and every imported product lands flat_bg_verified =
  false (kept out of the catalog) until the real feed and a real verifier exist.
  Do not read "realism" into these images.
-->

<rss version="2.0" xmlns:g="http://base.google.com/ns/1.0">
