    <!-- ========================================================================
         MODEST WEAR : the UAE market's everyday wardrobe
         ========================================================================
         Garments a real MENA feed carries and the generic Google taxonomy above
         does not describe: the abaya and the head coverings worn with it. Their
         feed categories name the garment, so they exercise the modest block of
         feed.category_map.

         Category mapping is an APPROXIMATION — see the comment on that block in
         config/feed.php. The engine has no head region, so the abaya goes to
         `dresses` (full-body one-pieces) and the head/shoulder coverings go to
         `upper_body` (the closest region it can dress).

         The khimar and niqab that briefly lived here are gone: a catalog photo
         must show the GARMENT ALONE (that is what flat_bg_verified means), and
         no such photo of either exists in the free stock libraries. A photo of
         a person wearing one is not a substitute — the engine would be handed
         the customer's photo plus a picture of a different woman. The mapping
         keys for both stay in config/feed.php, covered by XmlFeedParserTest, so
         a real feed carrying them still imports correctly.
         ======================================================================== -->

